{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"toolshed_web_search","tool":"call_web_search","arguments":{"web_search_instructions":"Prodigi Print API v4.0 sandbox create order product SKU t-shirt DTG API asset URL example"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Research Report: Prodigi Print API v4.0 Sandbox Create Order Product SKU T-Shirt DTG API Asset URL Example\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nThe Prodigi Print API v4.0 enables seamless integration of print-on-demand services into applications, allowing for the creation and management of orders, including direct-to-garment (DTG) t-shirt printing. Utilizing the sandbox environment, developers can test order creation processes without incurring costs, ensuring proper functionality before transitioning to the live environment.\n\n## Key Findings\n\n- **Finding 1:** Prodigi offers both sandbox and live environments for API integration, with the sandbox environment allowing for testing without actual fulfillment or charges. ([prodigi.com](https://www.prodigi.com/print-api/docs/reference/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Finding 2:** To create an order for a DTG t-shirt, developers must specify the appropriate SKU, provide recipient details, and include a publicly accessible asset URL for the design to be printed. ([prodigi.com](https://www.prodigi.com/blog/your-first-print-api-order/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Finding 3:** The API requires authentication via an `X-API-Key` header, which can be obtained by signing up for a free Prodigi account. ([prodigi.com](https://www.prodigi.com/print-api/docs/reference/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Finding 4:** Prodigi provides a Postman collection for API v4.0, facilitating easier testing and integration of API endpoints. ([postman.prodigi.com](https://postman.prodigi.com/?utm_source=openai))\n\n---\n\n## Detailed Source Analysis\n\n### Source 1: Prodigi API Documentation\n\n- **URL:** [https://www.prodigi.com/print-api/docs/reference/](https://www.prodigi.com/print-api/docs/reference/)\n\n- **Domain:** prodigi.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** Date not specified\n\n- **Source Type:** Official Documentation\n\n- **Credibility:** High (Official documentation from the service provider)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThe Prodigi API documentation provides comprehensive information on integrating print-on-demand services, including details on authentication, order creation, and environment configurations. It outlines the use of the `X-API-Key` for authentication and differentiates between the sandbox and live environments, emphasizing the importance of using the sandbox for testing purposes.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Sandbox API URL: `https://api.sandbox.prodigi.com`\n\n- Live API URL: `https://api.prodigi.com`\n\n- Authentication header: `X-API-Key`\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"Each request to our API requires the use of an authentication header: `X-API-Key`.\"\n\n> \"We have two environments: Sandbox and Live. Creating a new account on the Live Dashboard will automatically set up both a Sandbox and Live account.\"\n\n---\n\n### Source 2: How to Place your First Order with the Prodigi Print API\n\n- **URL:** [https://www.prodigi.com/blog/your-first-print-api-order/](https://www.prodigi.com/blog/your-first-print-api-order/)\n\n- **Domain:** prodigi.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** Approximately 5.4 years ago\n\n- **Source Type:** Blog Post\n\n- **Credibility:** High (Published by Prodigi)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThis blog post guides users through the process of placing their first order using the Prodigi Print API. It emphasizes the importance of selecting the correct product SKU, preparing the image asset with appropriate dimensions and format, and submitting the order via the API. The post also highlights the use of the sandbox environment for testing purposes.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Example SKU: `GLOBAL-FAP-16x24`\n\n- Image formats accepted: JPG and PNG\n\n- Sandbox environment recommended for testing\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"For the purposes of testing, we strongly recommend using the sandbox environment.\"\n\n> \"We accept jpg and png format images. For some products we may recommend one format over the other (e.g. apparel and device cases work best with png).\"\n\n---\n\n### Source 3: Prodigi API V4: Public Collection\n\n- **URL:** [https://postman.prodigi.com/](https://postman.prodigi.com/)\n\n- **Domain:** prodigi.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** Date not specified\n\n- **Source Type:** API Documentation\n\n- **Credibility:** High (Official documentation from the service provider)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThe Prodigi API V4 Public Collection provides a set of example API calls for clients, facilitating the integration and testing of the Prodigi Print API. It includes endpoints for order operations, quotes, and product details, and emphasizes the use of the sandbox environment for development and testing.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Sandbox API URL: `https://api.sandbox.prodigi.com`\n\n- Live API URL: `https://api.prodigi.com`\n\n- Authentication header: `X-API-Key`\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"Testing and development should be done against the sandbox API. This is an environment where you can create, and submit orders without incurring any costs.\"\n\n> \"All requests should be made over HTTPS. Connections cannot be made via HTTP.\"\n\n---\n\n## Cross-Reference Analysis\n\n**Consensus Across Sources:**\n\n- All sources agree on the importance of using the sandbox environment for testing API integrations without incurring costs. ([prodigi.com](https://www.prodigi.com/print-api/docs/reference/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- The necessity of authenticating API requests using the `X-API-Key` header is consistently emphasized. ([prodigi.com](https://www.prodigi.com/print-api/docs/reference/?utm_source=openai))\n\n**Conflicting Information:**\n\n- No conflicting information was identified among the sources.\n\n**Information Gaps:**\n\n- Specific examples of creating an order for a DTG t-shirt with a particular SKU and asset URL are not provided in the analyzed sources.\n\n- Detailed information on handling multiple assets for products with multiple print areas is limited.\n\n---\n\n## Research Metadata\n\n- **Search Completed:** 2026-08-24T05: "}],"_meta":{"openai/widgetSessionId":"7a9a412d-d5ff-4677-9715-9903b647fe1e"},"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
